            <div xml:id="d782">

                <pb facs="0999" n="885" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg885"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.51/107: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schuyler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-28T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>7. Department’s January 31, 6 p.m.</p>
                <p>Department informed that loan contract and purchase contract signed February
                    11th. You will therefore acknowledge note received from Foreign Minister as
                    previously instructed. Department desires that Government of Salvador should
                    reply taking note of <pb facs="1000" n="886" xml:id="pg886"/> fact that this
                    Government reserves liberty of action with regard to future diplomatic
                    representations as stated in your acknowledgment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
